  "label": {
    "en": ["Alphonso & Imogene: an idyl of Henry's Carbolic Salve [inscribed] — Flap Fold"]
  },
  "summary": {
    "en": ["A patent-medicine trade card with a single fold-up flap. The item has three surviving photographs: the front side collapsed, the front side fully opened, and the back side collapsed. The lower part of the front sheet hinges upward on one crease, and a different portrait printed on its verso covers the upper part when folded. This manifest references the original UCLA IIIF resources and supplies Web Annotation mark-up describing the fold geometry and behavior."]
  },
